  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Three charges $Q,+y$ and $+q$ are placed at the vertices of a right-angle isosceles triangle as shown below. The net electrostatic energy of the configuration is zero, if the value of $\\mathrm{Q}$ is\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ACMkbyx-gJKYcY_ZkGmz2yf3DeBJaTAYM4bYcnXGj14.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pk4MK",
      "text": "$+q$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FRCUo",
      "text": "$\\frac{-\\sqrt{2} q}{\\sqrt{2}+1}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sr8vb",
      "text": "$\\frac{-q}{1+\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "90HpU",
      "text": "$-2 q$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Net electrostatic energy for the system\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{K}\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{q}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{Qq}}{\\mathrm{a}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{Qq}}{\\mathrm{a} \\sqrt{2}}\\right]=0$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Ta7PcdFDTix28uAoxUaawKRwl8re3wKyVF-k34afOU8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\Rightarrow q &=-Q\\left[1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right] \\\\ & \\Rightarrow Q=\\frac{-q \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}+1} \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
